solution_md:
Let  $\overline{KZ}$  meet  $\overline{BC}$  at  $D$ , and let  $E$  be the orthocenter of  $\triangle ABC$ . We will show that  $\triangle KZX\sim \triangle KHB$ , from which the conclusion easily follows. First notice that  $ANOM$  and  $OMZX$  are concyclic. Therefore by spiral similarity, we have 
\[\triangle OZX\sim\triangle ONA\sim\triangle EHB.\] 
Now it suffices to show that  $\frac{EH}{KH}=\frac{OZ}{KZ}$ . Let  $G$  be the centroid of  $\triangle ABC$ , and let  $G'$  be the point on segment  $DZ$  such that  $\frac{HG'}{G'Z}=2$ . From the length condition, it is easy to see that  $KG\parallel BC$ . Moreover, 
\[\frac{DK}{KZ}=2=\frac{HG'}{G'Z},\] so  $KG'\parallel BC$  as well, and hence  $K,G,G'$  are collinear. Finally, since  $\frac{EG}{GO}=2=\frac{HG'}{G'Z}$ , we see that  $EO\parallel HZ$  as desired. 
