for the second inequality I have a simple solition:
the function  $f:(0,\infty )\to (0,\infty )$ ,  $f(x)=\frac{1}{x+1}$  it is a convex one.
Pick: $p_1=\frac{ab}{3}$ ,  $p_2=\frac{bc}{3}$ , $p_1=\frac{ca}{3}$  and $x_1=c$ ,  $x_2=a$ , $x_1=b$ . Apply $\sum_{i=1}^3 p_i f(x_i)\geq f(p_i x_i)$  and we are done.

