The function  $f$ , defined on the set of ordered pairs of positive integers, satisfies the following properties:
\begin{eqnarray*} f(x,x) &=& x,  f(x,y) &=& f(y,x), \quad \text{and}  (x + y) f(x,y) &=& yf(x,x + y). \end{eqnarray*}
Calculate  $f(14,52)$ .

solution_md:
Let the number be  $N$ . So  $N^3\equiv 8\pmod {10}$ , which means  $N\equiv 2\pmod {10}$ . Let  $N=10a+2$ . We have  $(10a+2)^3\equiv 88\pmod {100}$ , or  $a\equiv 4\pmod 5$ . Let  $a=5b+4$ . We have  $(50b+42)^3\equiv 888\pmod {1000}$ , or  $b\equiv 3\pmod 5$  (<details><summary>proof</summary>\begin{align*}
(25b+21)^3 &\equiv 111\pmod {125} 
3\cdot 25b\cdot 21^2+21^3-111 &\equiv 0\pmod {125} 
3\cdot 25b\cdot 21^2+(25-4)^3+14 &\equiv 0\pmod {125} 
3\cdot 25b\cdot 21^2+3\cdot 25\cdot 4^2-50 &\equiv 0\pmod {125} 
3b\cdot 21^2+3\cdot 4^2-2 &\equiv 0\pmod 5 
3b+1 &\equiv 0\pmod 5 
b &\equiv 3\pmod 5.
\end{align*}</details>). Let  $b=5c+3$ . So all numbers of the form  $250c+192$  satisfy the condition, the smallest positive one being  $250(0)+192=\boxed{192}$ .  $\blacksquare$

